# The package check - `hi --preview packages` renders what the priorities
# below do: each one's colors, a real example of each from this file, then
# the check itself. _HI_PACKAGES_MIN_PRIORITY (0-3) is the dial that decides
# how far down the list you want to hear about; it ships at 2, so tiers 0-1
# are hidden. Drop `check` from _HI_HEADER_ORDER to turn the check off.
#
# `hi --add-package` copies this file to ~/.config/say-hi/packages the first
# time and edits it there; that copy replaces this one wholesale.
#[-|+]package:priority,package2:priority2...
# a leading `-` speaks only when the whole line is missing, `+` only when one
# of it is installed; no flag speaks both ways. Priorities run 0-3, loudest
# last; on a line nothing satisfies, the max priority listed is the one used.

